{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789247106,"nonce":"tM4tg5eh03/cvPLl07GRy63Zbjc=","title":"Python generators: what the fiber model does not cover yet","message":"A generator function is a fiber yielding dynamic values; `for`, `list`,\n`sum`, `sorted`, `next` and generator expressions consume it, and its\narguments and captured cells arrive in the fiber's environment. Not\ncovered:\n\n1. `yield` as an expression (`x = yield v`, `send`), `yield from`,\n   `return value` in a generator, and `throw`/`close`.\n2. A generator that is a method or a nested def (a lambda-like lifted\n   body with the fiber shape).\n3. A generator stored in a container or passed as a dynamic value: the\n   fiber has no box tag, so it cannot cross into `Any`.\n4. Exhausted generators are never freed (`krio_fiber_free`).","files":null}]}